.\" rkllm - front end for the RKLLM runtime shipped by the rkllm-runtime package.
.\" Installed as /usr/share/man/man1/rkllm.1.gz
.TH RKLLM 1 "@DATE_ISO@" "rkllm-runtime @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rkllm \- run .rkllm models on Rockchip NPUs: local chat, one\-shot inference and an OpenAI\-compatible HTTP API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rkllm
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rkllm
.B chat
.I model
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rkllm
.B run
.I model
.I text
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rkllm
.B serve
.I model
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rkllm
.B list
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rkllm
.B info
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rkllm
.B selftest
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rkllm
is the command line front end for the RKLLM runtime that ships in the
.B rkllm\-runtime
package. It drives
.I librkllmrt.so
directly through ctypes and needs no compiler on the board and no Python
package from PyPI: it is written against the Python standard library only.
.PP
The runtime only executes
.I .rkllm
files, which must be produced on an x86_64 host with the RKLLM toolkit.
A
.I .rkllm
model is unrelated to the
.I .rknn
(vision) format.
.PP
The NPU is accessed through the
.I rknpu
kernel driver; this package neither ships nor builds that driver.
Use
.B rkllm info
to check that the driver is reachable.
Note that drivers from 0.9.x onwards do
.B not
create
.IR /dev/rknpu :
the NPU is registered as a DRM render node
.RI ( /dev/dri/renderD* ),
so look for
.I /sys/kernel/debug/rknpu/version
or a render node whose driver link points at rknpu, rather than for a device
node.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B chat
.I model
Interactive local chat. Reads prompts from standard input, prints the answer as
it is generated. The runtime keeps the conversation history, so each line is a
new turn.
.TP
.B run
.I model text ...
One\-shot inference: sends the given text and prints the answer to standard
output. Intended for scripts. No history is kept.
.TP
.B serve
.I model
Runs an OpenAI\-compatible HTTP API in the foreground. Does not read standard
input and does not offer an interactive prompt; a quiet terminal after the
startup banner is expected. See
.B HTTP API
below.
.TP
.B list
Lists the
.I .rkllm
files found in the model search path, and the search path itself when nothing
was found.
.TP
.B info
Reports the detected SoC, the frequency helper, the RKNPU driver status, the
loaded runtime library, the model search path and the models
found. Use
.B \-\-json
for machine\-readable output.
.TP
.B selftest
End\-to\-end self test that needs no model and no NPU. It exercises argument
handling, model resolution, the HTTP layer, streaming, authentication and queue
behaviour against a built\-in stand\-in engine. Checks that require the real
library and the NPU are reported as SKIP, not FAIL, when they are unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
Options may be given after the command in any order.
.SS Options common to chat, run and serve
.TP
.BI \-\-context " n"
Maximum context length in tokens. Default 4096. Do not set this above the limit
the model itself was converted with \- the startup log prints it as
.I max_context_limit .
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-new\-tokens " n"
Maximum number of tokens to generate per answer. Default 2048.
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " n"
Number of CPU cores used for inference. Default 4. On RK3588 and RK3576 the
four big cores (4\-7) are used; on other SoCs cores 0\-3.
.TP
.BI \-\-platform " soc"
Override SoC detection. One of
.IR rk3588 ", " rk3576 ", " rk3562 ", " rv1126b .
By default the SoC is read from
.IR /proc/device\-tree/compatible .
.TP
.BI \-\-model\-dir " dir"
Additional directory to search for models. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-lib " path"
Path to
.IR librkllmrt.so ,
for testing against a different build.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-freq\-lock
Do not raise CPU/NPU/DDR clocks before running. The lock helper is called by
absolute path as root and skipped otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-\-quiet ", " \-q
Suppress the startup banner and per\-request logging.
.SS Sampling options (chat, run and serve)
.TP
.BI \-\-top\-k " n"
Default 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-top\-p " p"
Default 0.9.
.TP
.BI \-\-temperature " t"
Default 0.8.
.TP
.BI \-\-repeat\-penalty " r"
Default 1.1.
.SS Additional options for chat and run
.TP
.BI \-\-system " prompt"
System prompt handed to the model's chat template.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-history
Do not retain the conversation context between turns.
.SS Additional options for serve
.TP
.BI \-\-host " address"
Address to listen on. Default 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces). Use 127.0.0.1 to keep
the API local.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
TCP port. Default 8080.
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-key " key"
Require
.B Authorization: Bearer
.I key
on every endpoint. Falls back to the environment variable
.B RKLLM_API_KEY
when the flag is absent. Prefer the environment variable: a value given on the
command line is visible in
.B ps
and in
.B systemctl status.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-queue " n"
Number of requests allowed to wait for the NPU. Default 32. The request that is
currently running does not occupy one of these slots. Requests beyond the limit
receive HTTP 503 with a
.B Retry\-After
header.
.TP
.BI \-\-queue\-timeout " seconds"
How long a request may wait for the NPU before being refused. Default 600.
.SS Options for list and info
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the report as JSON instead of text.
.SH MODEL RESOLUTION
A model argument is either an absolute or relative path to a
.I .rkllm
file, or a bare name. A bare name is looked up, with and without the
.I .rkllm
suffix, in the following directories in order:
.PP
.RS 4
.B $RKLLM_MODEL_DIR
(colon\-separated),
.IR /usr/share/rkllm\-runtime/models ,
.IR /var/lib/rkllm/models ,
.IR ~/.local/share/rkllm/models ,
and the current directory.
.RE
.PP
These directories are not created by the package, so that removing it leaves
nothing behind; create the one you prefer with
.BR mkdir \-p .
.SH HTTP API
.TP
.B GET /health
Service state: model name, whether inference is running, number of waiting
requests, uptime and counters. Does not touch the NPU.
.TP
.B GET /v1/models
OpenAI\-style model list.
.TP
.B POST /v1/chat/completions
OpenAI\-compatible completion endpoint. Accepts
.IR messages ", " model ", " stream ", " max_tokens ", " temperature ", "
.IR top_p ", " top_k ", " repeat_penalty ", " frequency_penalty ", "
.IR presence_penalty ", " enable_thinking " and " tools .
Streaming responses use server\-sent events and end with
.IR "data: [DONE]" .
.TP
.B POST /v1/reset
Forget the conversation context.
.PP
The same endpoints are also accepted without the
.I /v1
prefix, because clients disagree about whether it belongs in the base URL they
are configured with. For clients that expect a base URL, use
.IR http://host:port/v1 .
.SH AUTHENTICATION
If no key is configured the API is open. If a key is configured, every endpoint
requires
.B Authorization: Bearer
.I key
and answers 401 otherwise. The comparison is done in constant time.
.PP
The API speaks plain HTTP. A key keeps stray clients out but does not survive
packet capture; put a TLS proxy in front of it if the board is reachable from an
untrusted network.
.SH CONCURRENCY
The NPU serves one request at a time. Requests that arrive while the NPU is busy
wait in a queue of up to
.B \-\-max\-queue
entries and are refused with HTTP 503 beyond that.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RKLLM_API_KEY
API key for
.BR serve .
.TP
.B RKLLM_MODEL_DIR
Colon\-separated list of extra directories searched for models.
.TP
.B RKLLM_LIB
Path to
.IR librkllmrt.so .
.TP
.B RKLLM_<OPTION>
Every
.B serve
option can also be preset through the environment: the option name in upper case,
dashes turned into underscores, prefixed with
.BR RKLLM_ ,
so
.B RKLLM_TEMPERATURE
stands for
.BR \-\-temperature .
A flag given on the command line always wins. A value that does not parse is
reported on stderr and the built\-in default is used instead, so a typo in a
configuration file cannot stop the service from starting. This is the mechanism
the service unit's configuration file uses.
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
Not used by
.BR rkllm ;
it only affects how the Debian package is built.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/<triplet>/librkllmrt.so
The runtime library.
.TP
.I /usr/include/rkllm/rkllm.h
The C API header.
.TP
.I @SERVER_DEFAULTS@
Configuration for the systemd unit, and a
.I conffile
of this package: local edits survive an upgrade, and the file is deleted when
the package is removed. Every
.B serve
parameter has its own entry there, documented in English and in Chinese. It is
read by systemd, not by a shell, so there is no variable expansion. Apply a
change with
.BR "systemctl restart @SERVER_UNIT@" .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/@SERVER_UNIT@
Service unit for
.BR "rkllm serve" .
Shipped but never enabled or started by the package.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/rkllm\-fix\-freq\-<soc>
Frequency lock helpers called as root.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive chat:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
rkllm chat qwen2.5\-1.5b
rkllm chat /data/models/qwen2.5\-1.5b.rkllm
.RE
.fi
.PP
One\-shot, suitable for scripts:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
rkllm run qwen2.5\-1.5b "Summarise this text in one line."
.RE
.fi
.PP
API server with an API key, then a request from another terminal:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
RKLLM_API_KEY=sekret rkllm serve /data/models/qwen2.5\-1.5b.rkllm \-\-host 0.0.0.0 \-\-port 8080
curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/chat/completions \\
  \-H 'Content\-Type: application/json' \\
  \-H 'Authorization: Bearer sekret' \\
  \-d '{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hello"}]}'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Putting the key on the command line with
.B \-\-api\-key
is still accepted for one-off scripts, but that value then shows up in
.B ps
and in
.BR "systemctl status" ,
so the environment form above is the one to copy.
.PP
Verify an installation without a model:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
rkllm selftest
rkllm info
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error: model not found, library not loadable, inference failure.
.TP
.B 2
No command given; the usage message was printed.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C before completion.
.SH NOTES
A prompt far beyond the model's context window can make the runtime crash with
SIGSEGV, which takes the whole service down. Requests larger than eight bytes
per context token are therefore refused with HTTP 400 before they reach the
runtime. The check is a byte budget, not a token count, because no tokeniser is
available in this script.
.PP
Prompts are not tokenised here, so the
.I usage
figures in API responses are estimated by splitting on whitespace. Do not use
them for billing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR curl (1)
.PP
Documentation for the SDK itself is installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/rkllm\-runtime/ ,
and the upstream example sources under
.IR /usr/share/rkllm\-runtime/examples/ .
